place, Exod 2:4 (E, with מֵרָחוֺק ), 2Sam 18:13 (with מִנֶּגֶד ), figurative = stand aloof (VB Dr); 18:30 (with כֹּה , || עָמַד ): with ב loc, Exod 19:17 ; Num 22:22 (both E), Judg 20:2 ; Deut 31:14 (twice in verse), also (in sense of having a place or position ) יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּכָלגְּֿבֻל מֵהִתְיַצֵּב נִשְׁמַדְנוּ 2Sam 21:5 ; with בְּתוֺךְ person 1Sam 10:23 , location 2Sam 23:12 2Chr 11:14 ; with עַל location, at, by Num 23:3 , 15 (JE), upon Hab 2:1 (|| עמד ), Psa 36:5 (figurative); with עַל person see below; with שָׁם and עִם person Exod 34:5 (subject ׳י ), Num 11:16 (both J E). b. absolute 1Sam 3:10 ( ׳י subject); especially of standing quiet and passive, to see the mighty deliverance of ׳י Exod 14:13 (J), 1Sam 12:7 , 16 ; 2Chr 20:17 (|| עמד ); of taking a stand to fight 1Sam 17:16 ; Psa 2:2 ; in military array Jer 46:4 (with ב accompare), 46:14 (|| לָךְ הָכֵן ); to answer a charge Job 33:5 ; לְבוּשׁ כְמוֺ וְיִתְיַצְּבוּ 38:14 and they (terrestrial things) stand forth (in the light) like a garment . c. with לִפְנֵי person = present oneself before Exod 8:16 ; 9:13 (both J), Prov 22:29 (twice in verse); י ׳לִפְנֵי Josh 24:1 (E), 1Sam 10:19 (see also d ); so as servants or courtiers (see לְ 6c ), with implication of readiness for service עַלאֲֿדֹנָי Zech 6:5 ; י ׳לְ Job 1:6 ; 2:1 (twice in verse). d. with לְַ person take one's stand on the side of 2Chr 11:13 ; with עִם לִי מִייִֿתְצֵּב ל, Psa 94:16 who will take a stand forme against the workers of iniquity (|| עִם לִי יָקוּם מִי ); of holding one's ground , maintaining one's position before ׅ עֵינֶיךָ לְנֶגֶד ( ׳י 5:6 ; so with לִפְנֵי Josh 1:5 (D), Deut 9:2 ; Job 41:2 ; with בְּפָנֶיךָ Deut 7:24 ; 11:25 ; absolute לְהִתִיַצֵּב עִמְּךָ וְאֵין 2Chr 20:6","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 14","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 14","1Sam 3 10","1Sam 10 19","1Sam 10 23","1Sam 12 7","1Sam 12 16","1Sam 17 16","2Chr 11 13"],"related"